#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167699} :activity/id #uuid "a0121ff3-a1d1-5b12-b28a-eb686de0b7f2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048192 :topic/id #uuid "872dea5a-f6bb-5156-8b2e-6e50d5f47ed5" :topic/math-academy-id 3265} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167647 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166810 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166648 :question/id #uuid "c0e85144-6e01-5311-84d4-1042856272da" :question/math-academy-id "e-8456"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56fbaea3-3655-54cf-a3e1-5e0a5ce77c0d" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167429} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167430}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Hyperbolic Secant"} :step/id #uuid "ed9dbb0b-969b-5d04-9176-ed85ab2689bc" :step/math-academy-id 31488 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167719}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167648 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166811 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166649 :question/id #uuid "65b73c5e-690f-5ed6-b245-c96f2b61662a" :question/math-academy-id "e-8457"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "59907a9d-8d46-51d0-b568-0928211eb7e7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050125}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167427} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167428}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Hyperbolic Cosecant"} :step/id #uuid "b90ccf5a-43fc-5583-9208-20bd4902fb40" :step/math-academy-id 31489 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167718}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167649 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166812 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166650 :question/id #uuid "40c32ead-4f17-57d2-acd3-f65f6de1fe80" :question/math-academy-id "e-8458"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20904d6c-07bd-5e38-818d-17cb0d608dfb" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167431} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167432}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Hyperbolic Cotangent"} :step/id #uuid "7d44b52e-edbe-5a31-8008-e8abb5e89637" :step/math-academy-id 31490} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167699 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168089 :tutorial/content "$$\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nWe can define the **reciprocal hyperbolic functions** similarly to how we define reciprocal trigonometric functions.\n\nThe **hyperbolic cosecant function** (pronounced \"cosetch\") is defined as\n\n$$\n\\csch{x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sinh{x}} = \\dfrac{2}{e^x-e^{-x}}\\,\\,\\,\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=\\csch x$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/cc/cc0b2c19d1606c8a0a2c11411a0b0a4fbc09f264d9d28d0fcb2fb81f6c576a8a.png)\n\nNote the following properties of $y=\\csch x$:\n\n- Its domain is $x \\in (-\\infty, 0)\\cup (0,\\infty)$.\n- Its range is $y \\in (-\\infty, 0)\\cup (0,\\infty)$.\n- It is an odd function." :tutorial/id #uuid "81b4b2c8-5e07-5602-9aa1-a529be58c17b" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5205 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "08c055e4-f0a6-557f-8e3a-2c5a642e161a" :step/math-academy-id 32684 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167648}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167718 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168105 :tutorial/content "$$\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nThe **hyperbolic secant function** (pronounced \"sesh\") is defined as\n\n$$\n\\sech{x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\cosh{x}} = \\dfrac{2}{e^x+e^{-x}}\\,\\,\\,\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=\\sech x$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/b2/b228f9fba9d1b981d64730de4b3836de914e2565332780a3fd803c165fb7d2ba.png)\n\nNote the following properties of $y=\\sech x$:\n\n- Its domain is $x \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$.\n- Its range is $y \\in (0, 1]$.\n- It has the horizontal asymptote $y=0$.\n- It is an even function." :tutorial/id #uuid "efaf14f0-74f5-5f20-bd4f-eb1015699d33" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5353 :tutorial/title "Hyperbolic Secant"} :step/id #uuid "d5ff79b9-342e-5736-b506-5b930d5a43f8" :step/math-academy-id 33483 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167647}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167719 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168106 :tutorial/content "The **hyperbolic cotangent function** (pronounced \"coth\") is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\coth x = \\frac{1}{\\tanh x} &= \\frac{e^{x} + e^{-x}}{e^{x} - e^{-x}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=\\coth x$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/d3/d3d4f5cbe846f7725399fa1b1769c4f476be439575043537a2caa80c318a5ec9.png)\n\nNote the following properties of $y=\\coth x$:\n\n- Its domain is $x\\in (-\\infty, 0)\\cup (0,\\infty)$.\n- Its range is $y \\in (-\\infty, -1)\\cup (1,\\infty)$.\n- It has horizontal asymptotes $y=\\pm 1$.\n- It is an odd function.\n\nUsing the alternative definitions of $\\tanh x$, we can write down two more definitions for $\\coth x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\coth x &= \\frac{1}{\\tanh x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{e^{2x} + 1}{e^{2x} - 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 + e^{-2x}}{1 - e^{-2x}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "e64e0ad4-0bf1-549c-a2fd-9ac26f9049f6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5354 :tutorial/title "Hyperbolic Cotangent"} :step/id #uuid "ce8d00e0-fe25-5d82-8ae5-565d740702c0" :step/math-academy-id 33484 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167649}}] :activity/title "The Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186167031}]}
